{
  "sn40.10:0.1": "Linked Discourses 40.10 ",
  "sn40.10:0.2": "1. By Moggallāna ",
  "sn40.10:0.3": "With Sakka ",
  "sn40.10:1.1": "And then Venerable Mahāmoggallāna, as easily as a strong person would extend or contract their arm, vanished from Jeta’s Grove and reappeared among the gods of the thirty-three. ",
  "sn40.10:1.2": "Then Sakka, lord of gods, with five hundred deities came up to Mahāmoggallāna, bowed, and stood to one side. Mahāmoggallāna said to him: ",
  "sn40.10:2.1": "“Lord of gods, it’s good to go for refuge to the Buddha. ",
  "sn40.10:2.2": "It’s the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm. ",
  "sn40.10:2.3": "It’s good to go for refuge to the teaching. ",
  "sn40.10:2.4": "It’s the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm. ",
  "sn40.10:2.5": "It’s good to go for refuge to the Saṅgha. ",
  "sn40.10:2.6": "It’s the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm.” ",
  "sn40.10:3.1": "“My good Moggallāna, it’s good to go for refuge to the Buddha … ",
  "sn40.10:3.2": "",
  "sn40.10:3.3": "the teaching … ",
  "sn40.10:3.4": "",
  "sn40.10:3.5": "the Saṅgha. ",
  "sn40.10:3.6": "It’s the reason why some sentient beings, when their body breaks up, after death, are reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm.” ",
  "sn40.10:4.1": "Th